Anaga
-----

Another random crap I created on a weekend because I was bored and thought
"how hard can it be to write a kernel?" — turns out, pretty hard.

I think I made this like a year ago, but pushing now because YOLO.

A 32-bit x86 kernel written in C and assembly.

Building
--------

Requires nasm, i686-elf-gcc, i686-elf-ld, qemu-system-i386,
and probably more stuff than friends I have.

make
make run

